# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Pages reads this file from the root of the build output. Vite copies
# everything in public/ there, so this is the source of truth for it.
#
# The policy below is tight because the site genuinely earns it: no backend, no
# analytics, no fonts, no CDN, no embeds, not one raster image. A site with
# nothing third-party in it should say so in a header a browser will enforce,
# not only in prose on the landing page.
#
# Two allowances, and both are real rather than lazy:
#
#   style-src needs 'unsafe-inline' because the game pages carry a small inline
#   <style> block (they must style html/body before any stylesheet arrives, or
#   the canvas letterboxes against a white flash) and because the reveal
#   animations pass their stagger index as a style attribute. Hashing the block
#   would not help: style attributes are covered by the same directive and
#   cannot be hashed.
#
#   script-src is 'self' with NO 'unsafe-inline'. Vite extracts every inline
#   module into a hashed file, so nothing needs it. The JSON-LD blocks are
#   type="application/ld+json", which browsers do not execute and CSP does not
#   gate.
#
# img-src needs data: for the grain texture. It is an inline SVG noise filter
# in the CSS, not a file, and 'self' alone blocks it — measured, not assumed:
# the browser raised an img-src violation and the grain vanished silently,
# which is precisely the sort of thing that ships broken.
#
# Strict-Transport-Security is a year, with subdomains, and deliberately NO
# 'preload'. Preload is the one directive here that cannot be taken back: it
# is baked into browser binaries and removal takes months. A year of HSTS
# gets essentially all of the protection and stays reversible, which is the
# right trade for a site that may yet move to a custom domain.
#
# connect-src 'self' is the one that backs the privacy promise: the page cannot
# reach another origin even if something later tried to. It is 'self' rather
# than 'none' so a game can still load a sound file from this origin, which
# engine/audio.js supports and nothing uses yet.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; media-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; child-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), magnetometer=(), gyroscope=(), accelerometer=(), midi=(), serial=(), bluetooth=(), display-capture=(), idle-detection=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
